            <title>0.2.5</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 19 Mar 2026 22:44:38 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1773985272</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Chat attachment support — You can now drag and drop or paste files and images directly into the chat composer. Attachments appear as previews above the input field before sending.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Smarter tool groups in chat — Tool call groups now auto-expand while tools are running and show a live "Running N tools…" status. When all tools finish, the group automatically collapses after a short delay.</li>
<li>Faster project switching — Chat pane restoration is now deferred until after the window renders, so switching to a project with open chat panes feels significantly snappier.</li>
<li>Hardened Codex chat sessions — Codex chat turn completion now tracks per-message state, buffers stderr, and properly handles edge cases like process exits before stream completion, reducing stuck or blank chat turns.</li>
<li>Multiline chat composer rewrite — The chat input field now uses a proper text view with multiline editing, correct cursor positioning for unicode text, and support for paste and drop handlers.</li>
<li>Codex profile flag passthrough — Codex chat sessions now correctly forward model overrides and configuration flags (like --profile, --sandbox, --config) from your model profile commands.</li>
<li>Test runner pane ownership — When an agent triggers a test run, the Tests pane is now owned by and anchored to that agent, keeping test results associated with the pane that requested them.</li>
<li>Resilient chat conversation loading — Saved chat conversations now decode gracefully when fields are missing or have unexpected casing, preventing blank chat restores after updates.</li>
<li>Model profile deduplication — Duplicate built-in model profiles (e.g. multiple GPT-5.4 entries) are now automatically detected and cleaned up on launch.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Bug Fixes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Fixed pane corner radius highlighting not tracking the focused pane correctly when switching between panes — the selection indicator now updates reliably.</li>
<li>Fixed plan card titles getting clipped when hovering over action buttons — the header content area now adjusts its trailing constraint based on which trailing view is visible.</li>
<li>Fixed Cmd+click path injection in the file explorer not working when the row was already selected — the action now fires from the click handler instead of the selection delegate.</li>
<li>Fixed sidebar activity indicators showing stale state — they now reflect actual agent activity by polling the real pane model state.</li>
<li>Fixed sub-agent connector arrows flickering between directions — the arrow now uses the dominant center offset between parent and child panes for stable positioning.</li>
<li>Fixed background review agents getting permanently stuck — a 5-minute watchdog timer now fails wedged review processes so the parent agent can continue.</li>
<li>Fixed LSP diagnostics callback firing on a background thread, which could cause UI glitches in the footer status bar.</li>
<li>Fixed git snapshot operations not validating project paths before launching git, which could cause crashes with malformed paths.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
